    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0625" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg545"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Loomis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 402.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 564, of February 23
                    last, in regard to the visit of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Scorpion</hi> to Santa Catalina, I inclose for your information copy of a
                    letter from the Secretary of the Navy, pointing out the distinction existing
                    between the ordinary visit of a man-of-war and a visit for “scientific
                    purposes.”</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d506-a1.xml" xpointer="d506-a1"/>
            </div>
